@startuml 05-state-diagram-ticket-lifecycle
title Ticket Lifecycle (State Diagram)

[*] --> New : created by guided form\nor confirmed voice draft

New --> Triage : missing commissioning data\n(RULE_08) or low-confidence\nvoice draft needs review
New --> AwaitingInfo : evidence incomplete\n(missing error code / photo)
New --> Scheduled : party & priority assigned,\nvisit booked

Triage --> Scheduled : back-office verifies\nwarranty / party manually
AwaitingInfo --> Scheduled : missing evidence\nsupplied

Scheduled --> EnRoute : technician dispatched
EnRoute --> OnSite : technician arrives
OnSite --> AwaitingParts : part required,\nnot on the van
OnSite --> Resolved : fault fixed on this visit
AwaitingParts --> Scheduled : part received,\nre-booked

Resolved --> InvoicePending : chargeable == true
Resolved --> Closed : chargeable == false\n(warranty / contract / referred)

InvoicePending --> Closed : invoice issued

Closed --> Reopened : customer reports\nthe same fault again
Reopened --> Triage : re-enters triage;\nRULE_10 repeat-fault flag\nlikely applies

Closed --> [*]

note right of New
  Emergency tickets (RULE_01/RULE_02)
  skip this lifecycle entirely and are
  handled outside the ticketing flow —
  see 01-end-to-end-flow.
end note

@enduml
